FILE: vUX-cShapes.js
FEATURE: cshapes-rectangle-fixes
DATE: 2026-10-11
PRIOR STATE: as last committed (no uncommitted changes to this file before this feature)

REASON
Found while using animatedRectangle() as the animated border of the vilshub.com contact form.
The fixedRectangle() and animatedRectangle() sections are rewritten around two shared helpers
(prepareCanvas, strokeRectangle); the public API is unchanged apart from the new config.radius.

Fixed:
  1. iterationCount = <number> threw ReferenceError: it called validateinteger(), which does not
     exist. Now validateInteger().
  2. No beginPath() per frame: each frame added a rect to the path and re-stroked all of them,
     so the work per frame grew through every cycle. strokeRectangle() begins a path each time.
  3. Canvas drawn at CSS-pixel resolution, so blurry on high-density screens. prepareCanvas()
     sizes the backing store by devicePixelRatio and scales the context; drawing stays in CSS px.
  4. Restart: the loop identified itself by the canvas id, so draw() during a run started a
     second loop (double speed), and the progress == 1 branch restarted even after stop(). A run
     token (bumped by draw, stop, destroy) now ends any older loop on its next frame. The id
     requirement is dropped.
  5. Seamless loops: the dash offset moved 100px per cycle, which only loops cleanly when the
     dash period divides 100 (the default [10, 2] jumped). It now moves the whole number of
     periods nearest 100px (default: 96px; ProgressIndicator's [12, 5]: 102px).
  6. Cycle end was detected with eased progress == 1, so an easing not ending on exactly 1 never
     finished; and duration 0 produced NaN progress and stopped without the callback. Cycle end
     now uses the time fraction, and duration 0 counts as complete.
  7. clearRect() was offset by the origin, leaving a strip uncleared with a non-zero origin. The
     whole canvas is cleared.

Added:
  - config.radius (both shapes, number >= 0). A rounded path cannot sit on the canvas edge like
    the square one (its corners bend inward and would show the full width while the edges show
    half), so it is stroked at half the width, inset by a quarter: same visible thickness as the
    square case, all the way round. Square rectangles keep the original edge stroke, so their
    output is unchanged.
  - draw() paints the first frame synchronously, so stop() straight after draw() still leaves a
    still rectangle (needed because a stopped run no longer paints its pending frame).
  - destroy() is now listed as non-writable alongside draw and stop.

Verified headless (Chromium, deviceScaleFactor 2): numeric iterationCount 3 -> 3 callbacks then
stops; two extra draw() calls keep one loop (rAF count unchanged); canvas 400x240 for 200x120 CSS;
radius leaves corners clear and edges drawn; stop() keeps the frame, destroy() clears it;
duration 0 with 2 iterations -> 2 callbacks; validation errors for 2.5, -1, "4px"; canvas without
id draws. ProgressIndicator grid type still paints and moves. vilshub.com border correct at 1440
and 390 px, follows resizes, still under reduced motion. Not verified: Safari, Firefox.

